{#
   Where a reader goes after finishing.

   Two things, and they answer different questions. "Related" is *more like
   this* — same section, or sharing a label, ordered by how much it shares.
   "Older / Newer" is *the rest of the site*, in order, for somebody who wants to
   keep reading rather than to read about the same thing.

   Until feature 017 an article ended and that was it: a reader who reached the
   bottom had the browser's back button and nothing else. That is the single
   biggest thing a site can do to be read more, and it cost two queries.

   Everything here comes from published-only repository methods, so nothing that
   is not readable can be recommended.
#}
{% if related is not empty or previous or next %}
    <nav class="mt-12 border-t border-rule pt-8" aria-label="Read next">
        {% if related is not empty %}
            <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">More like this</h2>

            <ul class="mt-3 space-y-3">
                {% for article in related %}
                    <li>
                        <a href="{{ path('article_show', { slug: article.slug }) }}"
                           class="font-medium text-ink no-underline hover:underline">
                            {{ article.title }}
                        </a>

                        <span class="block text-sm text-muted">
                            {% if article.publishedAt %}
                                {{ article.publishedAt|date('j F Y') }}
                                <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
                            {% endif %}
                            {{ article.content|reading_time }} min read
                        </span>
                    </li>
                {% endfor %}
            </ul>
        {% endif %}

        {% if previous or next %}
            <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap justify-between gap-4 border-t border-rule pt-6 text-sm">
                {% if previous %}
                    <a href="{{ path('article_show', { slug: previous.slug }) }}"
                       class="max-w-[45%] text-accent no-underline hover:underline"
                       rel="prev">
                        <span class="block text-muted">&larr; Older</span>
                        {{ previous.title }}
                    </a>
                {% else %}
                    <span></span>
                {% endif %}

                {% if next %}
                    <a href="{{ path('article_show', { slug: next.slug }) }}"
                       class="max-w-[45%] text-right text-accent no-underline hover:underline"
                       rel="next">
                        <span class="block text-muted">Newer &rarr;</span>
                        {{ next.title }}
                    </a>
                {% else %}
                    <span></span>
                {% endif %}
            </div>
        {% endif %}
    </nav>
{% endif %}
